      "problem": "Find the value of $\\sin{270^\\circ}.$",
      "worked_solution": "The angle $270^\\circ$ is a quadrantal angle. Let's draw out the quadrantal angles on the unit circle.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14249810/assets/792a778286533d589a3410223aaf197b07e64ea77566042d7bb8ac13fbad9768.png)\n\nFrom the unit circle, we see that the angle $270^\\circ$ corresponds to the point $(0,-1).$\n\nSince the sine of the angle corresponds to the $y$-coordinate, we have $\\sin{270^\\circ} = -1.$",
